    "## 1. What is a Dataset?\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Concept\n",
    "A **dataset** is an organised collection of data, usually a table where each **row** is an observation (record / sample) and each **column** is an attribute (variable / feature) describing that observation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Example\n",
    "*Simple:* a class register – each row a student, columns = name, age, marks.  \n",
    "*Business:* here, each row is one telecom customer and the columns describe their plan, billing and whether they left.  \n",
    "*AI/ML:* a model learns patterns from rows to make predictions about new, unseen rows.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Implementation & 4. Output\n",
    "*(code below, output printed under each cell)*"
