    "### 5. Interpretation\n",
    "The data is a pandas `DataFrame` – a 2-D labelled table. Every row describes one customer and every column one attribute.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6. Insight\n",
    "The grain of the dataset (one row = one customer) must be known before any analysis; otherwise counts and averages are misread.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7. AI/ML Relevance\n",
    "ML models consume tabular data as a matrix of rows (samples) × columns (features). Understanding the *grain* prevents data leakage and wrong aggregations."
   ]
  },
