    "## 2. Features, Independent Variables & Dependent Variable (Target)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Concept\n",
    "A **feature** is an individual measurable property used as input to a model. **Independent variables** (predictors / X) are the inputs; the **dependent variable** (target / y) is the output we want to explain or predict.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Example\n",
    "*Simple:* predicting house price – area, rooms and location are independent variables, price is dependent.  \n",
    "*Business:* predict customer churn from contract type, tenure and monthly bill.  \n",
    "*AI/ML:* supervised learning learns `y = f(X)`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Implementation & 4. Output\n",
