    "## 3. Numerical vs Categorical Features\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Concept\n",
    "**Numerical** features are quantities on which arithmetic is meaningful (mean, sum). **Categorical** features describe groups/labels (nominal = no order, ordinal = ordered). A column stored as a number is not automatically numerical – e.g. `SeniorCitizen` is 0/1 but represents a *category*.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Example\n",
    "*Simple:* age = numerical; blood group = categorical.  \n",
    "*Business:* `MonthlyCharges` is numerical; `Contract` is categorical (ordinal).  \n",
    "*AI/ML:* categorical columns need encoding, numerical ones may need scaling.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Implementation & 4. Output\n",
    "*(code below, output printed under each cell)*"
   ]
