    "## 4. Discrete vs Continuous Features\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Concept\n",
    "**Discrete** numerical features take countable values (integers: counts). **Continuous** features can take any value in a range (measurements, money).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Example\n",
    "*Simple:* number of children = discrete; height = continuous.  \n",
    "*Business:* `tenure` (whole months) is discrete; `MonthlyCharges` is continuous.  \n",
    "*AI/ML:* influences the choice of plots (bar vs histogram) and transformations.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Implementation & 4. Output\n",
